    <section id="online-adaptation" class="section section--dark">
      <div class="container container--wide">
        <p class="section-kicker">Online adaptation</p>
        <h2>Corrective feedback in Rho's latent action space</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Offline task adaptation is limited by the states represented in its
          demonstration dataset. Rho addresses failures after deployment through an
          internal latent policy that predicts an observation-conditioned initial
          condition for the frozen flow-matching action generator. Corrected action
          chunks are inverted through the same discretized flow used for generation,
          producing latent targets for this lightweight module. The vision-language
          backbone and action expert remain frozen, so online learning changes where
          generation begins without rewriting the offline-trained controller.
        </p>
        <p class="section-intro">
          In Meta-World, 50 additional scripted-expert episodes per task raise
          average success from <strong>57.5% to 73.3%</strong> across six
          challenging tasks. On FR3 Duo, only 15 additional human-supervised
          episodes per task improve difficult edge-of-distribution configurations:
          test-tube assembly success rises from <strong>30.0% to 70.0%</strong>,
          and plug insertion rises from <strong>66.7% to 93.3%</strong>.
        </p>
